Generate the autocompletion script for todo for the specified shell.

The script calls todo itself for every candidate, so it keeps
working when the commands change and never needs regenerating.

bash:
  source <(todo completion bash)
  todo completion bash > /etc/bash_completion.d/todo

zsh:
  source <(todo completion zsh)
  todo completion zsh > "${fpath[1]}/_todo"

fish:
  todo completion fish | source
  todo completion fish > ~/.config/fish/completions/todo.fish

Usage:
  todo completion [bash|zsh|fish] [flags]

Flags:
  -h, --help              help for completion
      --no-descriptions   disable completion descriptions

Global Flags:
  -v, --verbose   verbose output
